NAME
    wmedit - text editor WM client (Path C phase 30)

SYNOPSIS
    wmedit [PATH] [SECONDS]

DESCRIPTION
    Open a 640x400 editor window over the file at PATH (defaults
    to /tmp/edit if omitted).  Missing files open as empty
    buffers — Ctrl+S creates them on first save.  SECONDS is
    the lifetime cap (default 600 = 10 minutes); Ctrl+Q exits
    early.

    Keys (only delivered when the window has keyboard focus —
    click into the window first):
      printable ASCII   insert at cursor (replaces selection)
      Enter             insert newline (replaces selection)
      Backspace / DEL   delete selection if any, else char before
      Tab               insert 4 spaces (replaces selection)
      Arrow keys        move cursor; clears any active selection
      Ctrl+S            save buffer to PATH
      Ctrl+Q            quit
      Ctrl+C            copy selection (or whole buffer if none)
      Ctrl+X            cut selection to clipboard
      Ctrl+V            paste clipboard contents at the cursor
                        (replaces selection if any)
      Ctrl+F            open search bar at bottom (session 152)
      Ctrl+Z            undo the last edit (session 153)
      Ctrl+Y            redo the last undone edit (session 154)

    Search mode (after Ctrl+F):
      printable ASCII   append to the search pattern; matches
                        highlight in mustard yellow inline; the
                        cursor jumps to the first match as you type
      Backspace         shorten the pattern
      Enter             jump to the next match (wraps to top)
      Esc               close the search bar; matches stop
                        highlighting but the cursor stays where it
                        landed

    Mouse: clicking places the cursor.  Click-and-drag selects a
    range; the highlighted bytes have a blue background.  Drag
    across rows for multi-line selection.  Caret is a 2-pixel
    vertical line that blinks while focused and no selection is
    active.

    The window title shows "wmedit  Ctrl-S save  Ctrl-Q quit"
    when focused.  The bottom status bar shows the path, a
    [*] marker if there are unsaved edits, and the current
    cursor position as "L<row>:<col> B<total-bytes>".

LIMITATIONS
    Single 8 KiB buffer cap.  No file picker yet (path is set
    at launch via argv[1]).  Search (session 152) is forward-
    only with wrap; no Shift+Enter "previous match" yet, no
    regex, no case-insensitive toggle.  Undo/redo (sessions
    153/154) coalesce typing bursts + backspaces into one
    step; a fresh edit clears the redo stack.  Per-entry text
    snap is 40 bytes, so undoing/redoing a very large
    selection-delete restores the cursor position but not the
    text content past 40 bytes.  Arrow-key
    support relies on the kernel's ANSI CSI passthrough for
    arrows (ESC '[' A/B/C/D), same path the shell uses for
    history navigation.

SEE ALSO
    wmtype(1), wmterm(1), wmd(1)
